llen: a modestly Democratic-leaning seat, incumbency, and an overwhelming money advantage over Jeanine Driscoll. Markets and most raters put the race in Likely D territory, so the forecast stays near the baseline with only a slight trim for the thin polling picture.", "watch": "A late surge of outside spending against Gillen or a strong national Republican environment on Long Island could tighten this into the Lean D range.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Laura Gillen (D) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term Democrat Laura Gillen seeks re-election in a Long Island district that leans about two points Democratic. She faces Republican Jeanine Driscoll, who won her primary in June but has raised only a fraction of what Gillen has. Gillen has emphasized local work on infrastructure funding and public safety, while the campaign has featured sharp exchanges over tax claims.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on fundamentals, expert ratings, and markets. Raters range from Tilt D to Safe D, and prediction markets give Gillen roughly a nine-in-ten chance. The race is rated Likely Democratic, with some room for movement if the national environment shifts.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9622, "margin": 11.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9401, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9422, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9272, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9344, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9323, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9557, "margin": 11.0}]}